SWEET Trusty TIPC GET_STATE (patch 0162, plan 2026-11-14 oneshot-2 step A5), boot-arg sweettrusty=2. Replays the stock Linux Trusty
driver path (kernel/google-modules/trusty 2494a3e, docs/research/50 sections 1-4): API version, FF-A init and RXTX_MAP, FF-A shares
(descriptor, 2 vrings, 4 rx buffers RW, 3 tx buffers RO), VIRTIO_GET_DESCR, VDEV_RESET, status ACK|DRIVER|DRIVER_OK, VIRTIO_START,
GO_ONLINE, one connect to com.android.trusty.gsa.hwmgr.aoc, HWMGR_CMD_STATE_CMD with GSA_AOC_GET_STATE (0) only, disconnect, then
VDEV_RESET, reclaims, VIRTIO_STOP, RXTX_UNMAP. Plan rule A-1 allowlist enforced per call (function id and arguments) in
bsd/dev/sweet_tipc.h; no call is retried with other arguments; every std-call <= 2 s, the run <= 10 s. Shared memory is one
KMA_PERMANENT contiguous allocation, never freed. Host test shim/tipc_host_test.c (fake Trusty). Lines "SWEET TRUSTY: hwmgr.aoc state=N"
(pass) or "SWEET TRUSTY: tipc stop ...", last "SWEET TRUSTY: tipc done ...". Without sweettrusty=2 nothing changes.

